-- title:
--   Lemma 3.4: inner covariance of generated causal algebras
-- statement:
--   All Lie algebras below are real and finite-dimensional, with their usual Hausdorff vector-space topology; brackets of subspaces denote real linear spans. Let $W$ be an invariant closed convex cone, $\tau$ an involutive automorphism with $\tau W=-W$, and $h_1,h_2\in\mathfrak g^\tau$. Let $\phi$ be an ambient inner automorphism generated by fixed elements, with $\phi h_1=h_2$. Define $\mathfrak g(W,\tau,h)$ as the Lie algebra generated by $(\pm W)\cap\mathfrak g^{-\tau}_{\pm1}(h)$. Then
--
--   $$\phi\bigl(\mathfrak g(W,\tau,h_1)\bigr)=\mathfrak g(W,\tau,h_2),\qquad
--   \mathfrak g(W,\tau,h_1)\cong\mathfrak g(W,\tau,h_2).$$
--
--   Pointedness, generating, and simplicity are not required. This is a structural statement used in the paper's classification of causal subalgebras.
-- source:
--   Classification of 3-graded causal subalgebras of real simple Lie algebras, arXiv:2001.03125v2, PDF p. 18, Lemma 3.4

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Next46_P05

